 "name": "Forests of Disaster",
 "type": "spell",
 "img": "modules/jjk5e/icons/techniques/disaster-verdure.svg",
 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Disaster Verdure — Innate Technique (1st level)</em></p><blockquote><p>You are born with an amazing power, with many possibilities, plant manipulation, allowing you to protect those you care about.</p></blockquote><p>Beginning at 1st level, Starting at 1st level, you have begun to understand the power of nature. You gain the ability to manipulate nature at will. You can cast <em>Druidcraft</em> at will and gain the following cursed techniques:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Binding Plants.</strong> As an action for 1 Cursed Energy, you can choose one target within 30 feet of you trapped by plants. The target must make a Strength saving throw, on a failure it will be restrained. It can make a Strength check to break free from the plants, on a success they are free from the binds, on a failure they remain stuck.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Piercing Roots.</strong> As an action for 1 Cursed Energy, you can raise a bunch of roots from the ground to strike a target. You force all creatures in a 50ft line to make a Dexterity saving throw, on a failure they take 1d12 piercing damage, on a success they take half as much damage. This damage increases to 2d12 at 5th level, 3d12 at 11th level, and to 4d12 at 18th level.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Wall of Roots.</strong> As a reaction for 1 Cursed Energy, you rise deep roots from the ground to defend yourself or allies from attacks. As a reaction to you or an ally being targeted by an attack, you spring forth a wall of roots 10 ft tall and 5ft wide. The wall has an amount of hit points equal to your Cursed Energy modifier times your proficiency bonus.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
   "chat": ""
  },
